            <ArticleTitle>Suitability of a chocolate agar-based medium for the transportation and long term storage of Neisseria gonorrhoeae isolates at room temperature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86-87</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0167-7012(17)30304-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.mimet.2017.11.011</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neisseria gonorrhoeae isolates were grown on chocolate agar slants comprising GC Agar Medium Base supplemented with 1% modified Kellogg's supplement and 1% beef blood hemoglobin. The bacterial growth was covered with sterilized paraffin oil. Cultures were used for transportation and storage of Neisseria gonorrhoeae for 3months at room temperature.</AbstractText>
